WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.230
Changes in your diet not
only affect you physically,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.350
physiologically inside,

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.950
but also mentally,
how well you think,

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.059
psychologically,
how well you feel.

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:14.339
But you’ll never know just
how good you can feel

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:19.380
until you put it to the test
and try eating healthy.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.290
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.570
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.170
Today we look at what plant
based foods have to offer

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.730
for the special dietary
demands of pregnancy.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:30.750
In our first story,

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.090
we compare the breast
milk of vegetarian

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.810
and non-vegetarian women.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.620
A&nbsp;completely plant-based diet
is suitable during pregnancy,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.969
lactation, infancy, and childhood --
a position echoed by the oldest

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:49.559
and largest association of
nutrition professionals in the world.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:52.110
Ask a couple hundred
health professionals though,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.100
and as few as one in
three appear to know it.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.190
Like any diet during pregnancy,
though, it should be well-planned,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.559
which means consuming large
amounts and a wide variety

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:04.449
of plant foods from
all the plant food groups,

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:05.970
including whole grains, legumes

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.770
(like soybeans, regular beans,
split peas, chickpeas, and lentils),

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.370
vegetables, fruits,
and nuts and seeds.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:14.850
Make sure to get enough calcium
from healthy plant-based sources

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.680
and sufficient vitamin D
from sun or supplements.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.190
And critically important,
make sure you get

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.530
a regular, reliable source
of vitamin B12.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.189
I have a video about B12 in
pregnancy and for kids here.

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:27.170
The two books I recommend
for raising plant-based families,

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:31.009
published by two of my favorite
evidence-based dieticians, are

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:33.500
Your Complete Vegan Pregnancy
by Reed Mangels

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.740
and Nourish,
co-authored by Brenda Davis.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.321
What data do we have
on the impact of vegan diet

00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:42.280
on pregnancy outcomes?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.040
The vegans had a significantly
lower gestational weight gain

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.780
by about six pounds
and lower birthweights,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.110
but just by a few hundred grams,
both about seven pounds each,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.010
within the normal range,
with no differences in the rate

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:58.890
of preterm birth, nor any significant
differences in the umbilical cord blood

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:03.500
B12, folate, or iron marker levels
between the study groups,

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.570
not surprisingly since the vast
majority of both groups were taking

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.390
prenatal vitamins, as they should.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.989
What about the composition
of breastmilk from those eating

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:14.300
vegan or vegetarian diet?

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.790
The systematic review has shown
that all non-vegetarian, vegetarian,

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:23.349
and vegan mothers produce breast
milk of comparable nutritional value.

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:25.030
Even omega-3's?

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:29.310
There was no difference in milk
DHA composition by diet group,

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.280
but that's not saying much since
over 80% of study participants

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.099
had milk concentrations of long
chain omega-3 DHA below target.

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:39.270
I talk about the best way
to get pollutant-free sources

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:43.090
in a previous video, which we'll
link down in the doctor's note

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.620
on NutritionFacts.org or
in the description on YouTube.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.300
The meat and egg industries like
to scaremonger about choline.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.400
But wait, this study was
written by someone

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.740
with no conflicts of interest.
Liar!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.290
Here's a corrected version.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.200
The 'Competing interests'
section has been updated.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.330
And surprise, surprise!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.840
The author is a member of a meat
industry funded advisory panel.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.430
The truth is there's just as much
choline in the breastmilk of vegans

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.569
as those who eat eggs or meat.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:17.690
There is something egg-free,
meat-free mothers may not

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.730
be passing on as much,
though: industrial pollutants

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.400
like the banned pesticide DDT
and cancer-causing PCBs.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.590
The highest levels were found
in the milk of fish-eaters,

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.549
and the lowest levels
found in vegetarians.

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:33.319
Even just cutting out meat
may cut DDT stores in half.

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:34.319
For example, here's the levels of
pesticides and carcinogenic PCBs

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:35.319
found in the breastmilk from two
sisters with different dietary habit.

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:36.319
The levels of DDT, DDE (a breakdown
product of DDT), dieldrin,

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:37.319
and beta-hexachlorocyclohexane
(two other banned pesticides),

00:03:37.319 --> 00:03:38.319
as well as PCBs, were
much lower in the milk fat

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:39.319
from the lacto-vegetarian
mother than in that

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.319
from the non-vegetarian sister.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.319
That's because these chemicals
build up in the food chain

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:42.319
in animal fat, our fat, as well
as any animal fat we eat.

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:43.319
What about mothers
who eat strictly plant-based?

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:44.319
Their milk is even less polluted.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:45.319
For almost every contaminant,
there was no overlap

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:46.319
in the range of scores,

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:48.439
meaning the highest (worst)
vegetarian value was lower

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:51.540
than the best (lowest) value
obtained in the U.S. sample.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.849
And by vegetarian here,
they mean women who eliminate

00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:58.490
all animal products from their diets,
including eggs and dairy.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:01.280
The one vegetarian mom
who had more than trace amounts

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.060
in her breastmilk had only been
veg for less than a year.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.849
But for some of these
other toxic pollutants,

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:10.970
the average vegetarian levels
were only 1 to 2% as high

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.890
as the average levels
in the United States.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:19.090
Breast is still best regardless of
the dietary pattern of the mother,

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.440
but nursing infants
of vegetarian women

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.350
whose diets are low
on the food chain --

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.900
in other words plant-based --

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.880
have the advantage of being
exposed to less chemical pollution.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.380
In our next story,

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.580
I recommend all pregnant
and breastfeeding women

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.550
follow the consensus guidelines

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.380
to get about 200mg
of preformed DHA

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.940
from a pollutant-
free source.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.870
A systematic review of
randomized controlled trials

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:46.820
of DHA supplementation of pregnant
and breast-feeding women

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:51.090
failed to find any clear and consistent
short or long-term benefit

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:56.229
for psychomotor, mental, visual
or physical development.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.520
Maybe DHA supplementation
during pregnancy has no effect

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.462
because the body isn't stupid and
protects the growth of the baby's

00:05:04.462 --> 00:05:08.810
brain by drawing off of maternal
stores of DHA, upregulating maternal

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.380
DHA synthesis, and preferentially
shuttling it to the fetus.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:17.819
But what if moms don't start out
with large maternal stores?

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:21.360
In other words, maybe DHA
failed to help women

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.580
who were already getting
enough, but maybe women

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.639
with very low intakes would benefit
from DHA supplementation.

00:05:28.639 --> 00:05:33.539
Well, first it's interesting to note
that even by 1978

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:36.600
researchers were suggesting plant-based
diets as the diet of choice

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.130
in the treatment of our
number one killer.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:42.130
But babies breastfed
by vegan moms

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:45.960
have significantly less DHA in
their bloodstream presumably

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.770
because the moms had significantly
less DHA in their breast milk.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:56.210
The question is whether these
differences are of any consequence?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.960
The growth and development of
vegan and vegetarian children are normal,

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.390
as long as they're getting their B12.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:05.569
No evidence that neural or
intellectual functions are impaired.

00:06:05.569 --> 00:06:08.259
In fact the two studies we have
on vegetarian kids

00:06:08.259 --> 00:06:12.020
showed that they had higher IQ's,
though that may have been

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.840
because their parents tended
to be better educated.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.289
But even though the kids seemed fine,
that doesn't rule out the possibility

00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:22.229
that there may be some
subtle differences

00:06:22.229 --> 00:06:24.310
in visual or neural
functioning.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:28.080
It would be interesting to compare
the function of babies getting

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.069
vegan breast milk levels versus
general population levels.

00:06:32.069 --> 00:06:38.520
You can see vegans had 14,
vegetarians 30, omnivores 37.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:43.620
This study compared zero
to 32, 64, and 96,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:50.389
and 32 worked better than zero, but
more than 32 didn't add anything.

00:06:50.389 --> 00:06:53.780
This could explain why the general
population at 37 doesn't benefit

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.930
from additional DHA supplementation.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.060
But what about down at 14?

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:05.350
Most studies down at that level
showed no advantage over zero,

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:09.420
though one study found a benefit
supplementing at as low as 5,

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.999
but that doesn't help us.

00:07:11.999 --> 00:07:15.650
Now just because babies
breastfed by vegan moms

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:19.430
have significantly lower DHA
levels in the blood

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.629
doesn't necessarily mean they
have lower levels in their brain,

00:07:22.629 --> 00:07:24.550
which is where it counts.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:27.660
What we need is a randomized,
controlled trial in non-fish eaters

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:33.160
of DHA supplementation. Until then,
it's going to remain uncertain.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.990
So what should pregnant
and breastfeeding women

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.879
who avoid fish do
in the meanwhile?

00:07:37.879 --> 00:07:40.710
Low intakes of DHA
doesn't necessarily equate

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.500
with fetal DHA inadequacy,

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:48.720
but this new data suggests that some
infants may not be getting enough

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.430
and could benefit from
their moms supplementing.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.229
And so I recommend pregnant
and breastfeeding women

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:58.450
on plant-based diets do follow
the consensus guidelines

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.610
to get about 200mg of preformed DHA
from an uncontaminated source

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:09.759
like algae oil, which is probably
the best combination for all women

00:08:09.759 --> 00:08:13.460
given the state of our world,
to minimize exposure

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:20.849
to toxic pollutants such as
dioxins, PCBs, and mercury.

00:08:20.849 --> 00:08:21.849
Finally today,

00:08:21.849 --> 00:08:30.199
we look at the optimal B12 dosage
for kids, pregnant women, and seniors.

00:08:30.199 --> 00:08:33.149
Universal improvement of B12 status
appears “to be a nutritional

00:08:33.149 --> 00:08:37.039
imperative with possibly
profound beneficial effects,”

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:41.789
particularly at the bookends
of life—at old age and infancy.

00:08:41.789 --> 00:08:44.660
I’ve explained the rationale
for my recommendations

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:48.590
to take vitamin B12 supplements
once a week or once a day,

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:53.290
or alternately eat sufficient
daily B12-fortified foods.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:58.720
But for those over age 65 those
guidelines go out the window.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.140
The recommendations change
to everyone taking

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.800
a high daily dose of
1,000 mcg every day.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:09.160
Starting at age 50 everyone,
meat-eaters and vegans alike,

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:12.820
should be taking B12 supplements
or eating B12-fortified foods.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:20.920
But over age 65, 50 a day may not do it.
Even 100 a day doesn’t seem sufficient.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.530
Researchers investigated three
doses and found that most

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:28.019
didn’t normalize their MMA until
after the 1,000 microgram dose.

00:09:28.019 --> 00:09:31.610
(MMA suppression is a
measure of B12 sufficiency.)

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:37.730
But they just tested 25, 100, and 1,000.
Maybe 250 or 500 would do it?

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.981
Researchers set out to find an
adequate dose at that age,

00:09:39.981 --> 00:09:45.700
and it seems we need at least about
650 to 1,000 a day in most people,

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:49.370
hence my 1,000 a day
recommendation after age 65.

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:52.470
OK, what about the other
end of the life cycle?

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:56.019
The consequences of B12 deficiency
and insufficiency can be

00:09:56.019 --> 00:09:59.029
devastating in
infancy and childhood,

00:09:59.029 --> 00:10:01.459
and this is not just a problem
for plant-based pregnancies.

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:04.760
“Vitamin B-12 insufﬁciency during
pregnancy is common

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.950
even in nonvegetarian populations.”

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.730
About a quarter of all pregnant
women aren’t getting enough B12,

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:15.250
and that number rises to nearly
one in three by the third trimester.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:19.850
But, insufficiency isn’t as
bad as frank deficiency,

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.459
which can manifest in
cases like cerebral atrophy,

00:10:23.459 --> 00:10:24.890
meaning brain shrinkage,

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:29.660
in a “Vitamin B12-deficient
Infant of a Vegetarian Mother.”

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.440
Thankfully, even severe
brain atrophy can be

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.640
substantially reversed with
B12 supplementation,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:40.510
but better not to become
deficient in the first place.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.470
The solution proposed by a group
of French pediatricians

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:47.140
is to recommend against
raising vegan kids at all,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.399
since B12 supplementation is
necessary. And they’re not alone.

00:10:51.399 --> 00:10:54.100
To vegan or not to vegan.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:58.070
In 2016, two professional
organizations, the U.S. Academy

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:01.149
of Nutrition and Dietetics and
the German Nutrition Society,

00:11:01.149 --> 00:11:03.010
issued conﬂicting statements.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:06.280
The U.S. Academy said that
even strictly plant-based diets

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:09.529
are appropriate for all
stages of the life cycle,

00:11:09.529 --> 00:11:12.639
whereas the German group
echoed the French group,

00:11:12.639 --> 00:11:15.861
saying since you have to take B12
we can’t recommend a vegan diet

00:11:15.861 --> 00:11:20.950
for pregnant women, lactating women,
infants, children, or adolescents.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.230
To confuse the matter further,
the American Academy of Pediatrics

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:27.700
appeared to have it both ways;
in one place repeating

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:31.010
the U.S. Academy’s position, while
in another place it stated that

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:33.370
vegan diets should not
be recommended for children.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.610
But I think they’re just
saying the same thing.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:40.630
Everyone agrees that a non-B12
supplemented plant-based diet

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:45.360
is a bad idea—that’s part of what
the U.S. Academy means

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.430
by “well-planned.”

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.139
Everyone eating plant-based,
but especially pregnant

00:11:51.139 --> 00:11:56.279
and breastfeeding women, must
ensure a regular, reliable source

00:11:56.279 --> 00:12:01.350
of vitamin B12, meaning B12
supplements or B12-fortified foods.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:05.580
But then you may be able to
get the best of both worlds.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.670
That’s why there are
reviews with titles like this:

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:12.070
plant-based pregnancies:
danger or panacea?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.070
Danger if you don’t take your B12,
but “following a plant-[based] diet

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:19.930
during pregnancy may be protective
against the development of preeclampsia,

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:24.519
pre-gravid obesity, and minimize the
exposure to [DNA-damaging] agents.”

00:12:24.519 --> 00:12:28.660
It may also protect our newborns
“from the onset of pediatric diseases,

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.130
such as pediatric wheezing,
diabetes, neural tube defects,

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:34.959
orofacial clefts, and some
pediatric tumors.”

00:12:34.959 --> 00:12:37.779
“Vegan pregnant women
have a lower-than-average

00:12:37.779 --> 00:12:41.550
rate of cesarean section,
less postpartum depression,

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.110
and lower neonatal and
maternal mortality,

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:49.399
with no complications or negative
outcomes that are higher than average.”

00:12:49.399 --> 00:12:52.779
In addition, a lower incidence
of what used to be called toxemia,

00:12:52.779 --> 00:12:57.350
a potentially dangerous pregnancy
complication known as preeclampsia.

00:12:57.350 --> 00:13:01.550
“Overall, plant-based diets
seem to confer protection to both

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.519
mothers and newborns” by not
only “reducing the risk of several

00:13:05.519 --> 00:13:10.570
pregnancy-related issues”, but
decreasing the risk of childhood disease.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:13.900
“Children following plant-based
diets might have a lower risk

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.959
of developing obesity,” obviously
are less exposed to drugs

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.470
used in animal production,
and a favorable

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:23.500
anti-inﬂammatory proﬁle
of cell-signaling factors.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:28.880
But again, everyone on a plant-based
diet has to get enough B12.

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.139
Pregnant and breastfeeding
women can just follow

00:13:30.139 --> 00:13:33.899
my 50 micrograms a day
recommendation for nonpregnant adults,

00:13:33.899 --> 00:13:37.089
or 2,000 a week, though they
suggest breaking up those doses

00:13:37.089 --> 00:13:41.100
into two halves to boost absorption.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:45.470
After infants are weaned, they
can start on 5 micrograms a day;

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.699
from ages 4 through 10 they can
take half the adult dose of 25 a day;

00:13:48.699 --> 00:13:51.120
and then at age 11 they can
take 50 a day or 2,000 a week.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.740
You don’t have to worry
about taking too much.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:14:01.949
It’s water-soluble and you’ll
just end up with expensive pee.

00:14:01.949 --> 00:14:04.140
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:07.490
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.990
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:13.410
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:19.100
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:21.800
please go to the NutritionFacts
Podcast landing page.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:24.380
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.440
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.970
My last two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.160
and the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.480
Get ready this year for the
launch of How Not to Age.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.019
And, of course, all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:43.010
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.290
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.829
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:14:46.829 --> 00:14:51.029
on the latest in nutrition research
with bite-sized videos and articles

00:14:51.029 --> 00:14:54.010
uploaded nearly every day.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.510
Everything on the
website is free.

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.389
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorships,

00:14:57.389 --> 00:14:58.389
no kickbacks.

00:14:58.389 --> 00:15:01.060
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:04.550
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.050
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.508
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

